(***        Standard job list of a 1:1 configuration        ***)
(Copy this file into the directory Templates/Manufacturer or   )
(Templates/User and change the name into _TEMPL_, e.g.         )
(_TEMPL_.JOB or, if it is to exist in several languages, into  )
(_TEMPL__<language>, e.g. _TEMPL__GR.JOB.                      )
(Adapt this job list to your individual requirements.          )
(**************************************************************)
(A job list is executed with transfer direction MMC -> NC if   )
(the job list itself or a workpiece with a job list is loaded  )
((softkey Load) or selected (softkey Select). Unloading of a   )
(job list or workpiece with a job list causes execution with   )
(transfer direction NC -> MMC.                                 )
(                                                              )
(Loading instructions LOAD:                                    )
(--------------------                                          )
(The files are shifted in the direction of the transfer        )
(                                                              )
(LOAD *   loads all files from the workpiece of the job list   )
(LOAD /MPF.DIR/*    loads all files from a directory, here e.g.)
(                   all files from part programs  (MPF.DIR)    )
(LOAD PART1.MPF     loads a file, e.g. PART1.MPF               )
(                   from the workpiece of the job list         )
(LOAD /SPF.DIR/PART1.SPF  loads a file from the directory      )
(                                               Subprograms    )
(                                                              )
(Selection instruction SELECT:                                 )
(-----------------------                                       )
(The SELECT instruction is executed only with selection of the )
(workpiece or job list. The selected program must have been    )
(loaded before into the NC by means of LOAD.                   )
(Exception: Execution from hard disk.                          )
(                                                              )
(Command: SELECT name CH=<channel number>  [DISK]              )
(name: Name of the main program which is selected for execution)
(      in a specific channel in the NCK                        )
(DISK (optional) : For execution from hard disk                )
(SELECT PART2.MPF CH=2                                         )
( => PART2 is selected in the 2nd channel for execution        )

